## 1. Result Up Front

The short seam test did not find a positivity wall.  Once the complete
five-band action is Schur-eliminated, both the minimal-frame control and the
Block-188 orbit frame have an exact action-derived positive boundary port.
What fails is narrower: neither normalized stationary graph intertwines the
plain one-site spatial shift inherited from the frozen `d_00` chart.  The
action itself fails that same shift test.  This is a common-differential/chart
typing wall, not a reason to spend more time manufacturing positive matrices
on the two-dimensional carrier.

The campaign therefore executed the intended four-dimensional pivot.  On the
full exterior algebra of four directions, it constructs one finite-Laurent
Dirac--Kahler action, its ten metric vertices, and its reciprocal matter
recoil.  Their total first-order Ward identity cancels coefficient by
coefficient.  At three nonzero static spatial momentum strata, the same
vertex reaches both positive gravity TT directions as a rank-two operator
image.

A finite candidate family of local form-occupation measurement contexts also
separates the mass--Hodge parts of those two operator directions.  The
distinction matters:

- the union of seven contexts has rank `(2,2,2)` on axis, face, and body
  representatives;
- the single coordinate-occupation context has only `(1,1,2)`; and
- total form-degree marks have only `(0,1,0)`.

Thus the result does **not** say that one fixed commuting event partition reads
both polarizations everywhere.  On the axis representative, every one of the
seven displayed contexts has rank one; rank two is obtained only after
combining incompatible contexts.  More importantly, every displayed mark
preserves form degree, whereas the derivative/recoil part of the TT vertex
changes form degree by one.  The marks therefore see only the mass--Hodge
term, not the Ward/recoil dynamics.  This fits the framework's possibility
that a neighboring condition specifies a measurement partition, but it does
not derive which condition, partition, outcome probability, or permanent
write is realized.

The result is significant upstream common-action progress.  It is not a
retained end-to-end theory and does not move a TOE percentage.

