## 3. The Full-Band Bi-Schur Gate

On the four-slice antiperiodic quotient, fix the history and environment cuts
before inspecting a Gram:

\[
 N=\{0,\ldots,7\}\quad(t=0,1),\qquad
 P=\{8,\ldots,15\}\quad(t=2,3).                  \tag{1}
\]

The cover action is first reconstructed as the sum of all live temporal
bands,

\[
 Q^{(5)}=\sum_{\Delta=-2}^{2}\Pi_\Delta Q,         \tag{2}
\]

and only then descended.  This order is necessary because the distance-two
bands alias on the four-slice quotient.  Write the descended action as

\[
 q=\begin{pmatrix}A&B\\C&D\end{pmatrix}.           \tag{3}
\]

Every displayed block has rank eight on both frames.  Since `D` is invertible,
the normalized right and left stationary graphs are

\[
 V_R=E_N-E_PD^{-1}C,
 \qquad
 V_L=E_N-E_PD^{-T}B^T,                             \tag{4}
\]

with Schur operator

\[
 S_N=A-BD^{-1}C.                                   \tag{5}
\]

The exact identities are

\[
 qV_R=E_NS_N,
 \quad V_L^Tq=S_NE_N^T,
 \quad V_L^TqV_R=S_N,
 \quad(q^{-1})_{NN}=S_N^{-1}.                      \tag{6}
\]

The left/right distinction is real: `V_R-V_L` has 16 nonzero entries and rank
eight in both frames.  Treating this nonsymmetric fermion action as if one
right graph served both sides would erase the interface the calculation is
meant to test.

Let `R` be the descended projective reflection, define the dual-adjoint action
and honest doubled reflection by

\[
 \widetilde q=(RqR^T)^T,
 \quad
 \mathcal Q=\operatorname{diag}(q,\widetilde q),
 \quad
 \mathcal S=\begin{pmatrix}0&R^T\\R&0\end{pmatrix},
 \quad
 \mathcal K=\mathcal S\mathcal Q^{-1}.             \tag{7}
\]

For either stationary graph, the reflection-parity ports are

\[
 \mathcal V_\pm(V)=
 \begin{pmatrix}V\\ \pm R\overline V\end{pmatrix}.
                                                               \tag{8}
\]

The runner proves `K=K^dagger`, both compressed Grams are Hermitian of rank
eight, all eight leading principal minors of
`V_+^dagger K V_+` are positive, and the negative-parity Gram is negative
definite.  Positive position-space ports therefore exist without a fitted
eigenvector or a post-hoc absolute value.

The first empty interface is the inherited frozen-chart spatial action.  For
the descended one-site shift `U_x` and its restriction `u_N`,

\[
 [q,U_x]\ne0,
 \qquad U_xV_{R,L}-V_{R,L}u_N\ne0.                 \tag{9}
\]

The exact `(nonzero entries,rank)` values are `(160,16)` for the action and
`(48,8)` for each graph, on both frames.  This is not a general covariance
failure: a chart-family action, transported common differential, changed cut,
or paired source action is outside the tested class.

## 4. Genuine Four-Dimensional Exterior Carrier

Let `c_mu` be exterior creation and `a_mu=c_mu^T` annihilation on
`Lambda^*(R^4)`, dimension 16.  The runner constructs every matrix and checks

\[
 \{c_\mu,c_\nu\}=0,
 \qquad \{a_\mu,c_\nu\}=\delta_{\mu\nu}I.          \tag{10}
\]

At centered lattice momentum `k`, define

\[
 d(k)=\sum_{\mu=0}^{3}\sin k_\mu\,c_\mu,
 \qquad
 Q(k)=mI+i\bigl(d(k)+d(k)^T\bigr),
 \qquad m={2\over7}.                              \tag{11}
\]

Nilpotency `d(k)^2=0` follows from (10) and is checked independently.  The
Hermitian part is exactly `mI`, so the two declared action matrices have rank
16.  Positive mass is an accretivity/invertibility control, not an on-shell
matter-state construction.

For a transfer `q`, put

\[
 C_\mu(k,q)=\cos(k_\mu+q_\mu/2).                  \tag{12}
\]

In the same Frobenius coordinate order as the gravity action, the ten Hodge
vertices are

\[
 H_{\mu\mu}=C_\mu^2\left({I\over2}-c_\mu a_\mu\right),
                                                               \tag{13}
\]

\[
 H_{\mu\nu}=-{C_\mu C_\nu\over\sqrt2}
 (c_\mu a_\nu+c_\nu a_\mu),\qquad \mu<\nu.       \tag{14}
\]

The action vertex maps the incoming matter mode `k` to `k+q`:

\[
 V_A(k,q)=mH_A+i\left(H_Ad(k)+d(k+q)^TH_A\right). \tag{15}
\]

These formulas are the derivative of one displayed action family.  They are
not a pasted stress tensor.

## 5. Exact Total Ward Identity With Recoil

Let the centered gravity incidence be

\[
 g_\mu(q)=2\sin(q_\mu/2),                           \tag{16}
\]

and let `Gamma(q)` be the standard symmetric-tensor gauge map used by the
canonical gravity action.  For gauge direction `r`, define

\[
 \iota_r=C_r a_r,
 \quad L_r=d(k+q)\iota_r+\iota_r d(k),
 \quad \bar L_r=\bigl(d(k)\iota_r+\iota_r d(k+q)\bigr)^T.       \tag{17}
\]

The Hodge-level identity is

\[
 \sum_A\Gamma_{Ar}H_A=\bar L_r-L_r.                \tag{18}
\]

Using nilpotency, (18) gives the total off-shell first-order identity

\[
 \sum_A\Gamma_{Ar}V_A
 +Q(k+q)L_r-\bar L_rQ(k)=0                         \tag{19}
\]

for all four gauge directions.  The relative minus sign in the centered
left-recoil convention is load bearing.  With raw Laurent variables

\[
 z_\mu=e^{ik_\mu},\qquad u_\mu=e^{iq_\mu},         \tag{20}
\]

define the raw recoil insertions by

\[
 R_r=-i u_r^{1/2}L_r,
 \qquad \bar R_r=+i u_r^{1/2}\bar L_r.             \tag{21}
\]

The standard tensor/vector slot placements used by the runner define the raw
gravity--vertex contraction by

\[
 \sum_A\widetilde\Gamma_{Ar}\widetilde V_A
 =-i u_r^{1/2}\sum_A\Gamma_{Ar}V_A.
\]

The raw placed identity is therefore

\[
 \sum_A\widetilde\Gamma_{Ar}\widetilde V_A
 +Q(k+q)R_r+\bar R_rQ(k)=0.                        \tag{22}
\]

The mixed action derivatives have the ordinary plus-plus variational form in
raw placement while reducing exactly to the centered minus identity (19).

