## 7. Candidate Local Mark Contexts

The local coordinate occupation operators are

\[
 N_\mu=c_\mu a_\mu.                                \tag{24}
\]

For every unordered pair `(mu,nu)`, define the rotated mode occupations

\[
 N_\pm^{\mu\nu}={1\over2}\left(
 N_\mu+N_\nu\pm(c_\mu a_\nu+c_\nu a_\mu)\right).  \tag{25}
\]

Each pair context consists of `N_+`, `N_-`, and the two untouched coordinate
occupations.  The runner proves that every operator is idempotent and every
pair within one context commutes.  Together with the coordinate context this
gives seven fixed contexts.  Nothing is chosen separately for axis, face, or
body momentum.

